      "math_academy_id": "e-4978",
      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(2, -1)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x)$. Which point must lie on the graph of $y= -f(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The transformation $y=-f(x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(2, -1)$ lies $1$ unit *below* the $x$-axis. So, under the action of the transformation, this point will be reflected $1$ unit *above* the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217907/assets/5fc11d4ceb5ce0a1c9e7cd95fed19a07b3b3a78185f7dd8131f069bcdcc4bb1a.png)\n\nWe conclude that the point $(2,1)$ must lie on the graph of $y=-f(x).$",
